# State & API

## Data flow

```
Page → hook (useQuery/useMutation) → api/*.ts → axios (real) or Zustand store (mock)
```

## React Query defaults

- `staleTime`: 5 min, `retry`: 1, `refetchOnWindowFocus`: false
- Mutations: `retry: 0`; invalidate domain keys on success
- Paginated lists: use `placeholderData: keepPreviousData` to avoid unmounting UI during refetch

## Zustand

| Store | Persist | Purpose |
|-------|---------|---------|
| `authStore` | Yes | JWT + user + refresh token; `impersonationActive` flag |
| `organizationStore` | Yes | Active org switcher |
| Domain stores | No | Mock CRUD until backend wired |

- Auth store key: `auth-storage`; rehydrate sets `isAuthenticated` when token exists
- Impersonation backup: `sessionStorage` key `impersonation-backup` (super-admin session before switch)
- Domain stores hold `DEFAULT_*` seed data; mutated by mock API modules

## API status

**Real (axios):** `authApi`, `settingsApi`, `organizationApi`, `usersApi` (`/members`), `adminApi`, `invitationsApi`

**Mock (store + delay):** `screensApi`, `playlistsApi`, `mediaApi`

## Axios (`lib/axios.ts`)

- Base URL: `VITE_API_URL` or `/api/v1` (backend is versioned — see `project-overview`)
- Attaches `Bearer` token from `authStore`
- Unwraps `{ success, data }` envelope from backend responses
- On 401: attempts token refresh, then logout + redirect to `/login`
- Sends `Accept-Language` and `X-Organization-Id` (when active org set) on every request
- `resetAuthRefreshState()` — call before impersonate start/exit to avoid refresh races

## Mock → real migration

Replace store calls in `api/*.ts` with axios calls; keep the same function signatures and return types so hooks stay unchanged.
